python-activitytrack (0.9.9-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.9.9, in step with ActivityTrack 0.9.9: the PC learns of newer
    versions from the paired server, which relays a signed manifest (JWS,
    ES256 or RS256) checked against the key pinned from the pairing link (the
    link may carry k, the fingerprint of the server's key); the package is
    downloaded with its sha256 checked, never for an installation of the
    package manager. The unsigned check of the GitLab releases is gone. Wire
    schema unchanged (1, translated by the server).

 -- ActivityTrack <flavio-claude@zipman.it>  Sun, 08 Nov 2026 04:00:00 +0000

python-activitytrack (0.9.8-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.9.8, in step with ActivityTrack 0.9.8: the first release from
    GitLab. The update check reads the GitLab releases (a version with a
    suffix is a beta) and gets its first tests; the project's addresses move
    to gitlab.com/infraconsulting. Wire schema unchanged (1, translated by
    the server).

 -- ActivityTrack <flavio-claude@zipman.it>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 16:30:00 +0000

python-activitytrack (0.9.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

